import java.util.*;
import java.lang.*;

class Solution {
    public String antiShuffle(String s) {
        String[] words = s.split(" ");
        StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();

        for (String word : words) {
            char[] chars = word.toCharArray();
            Arrays.sort(chars);
            result.append(new String(chars)).append(" ");
        }

        return result.toString().trim();
    }
}
```

This Java method splits the input string into words, sorts each word's characters, and then joins them back together with spaces in between. The `Arrays.sort(chars)` line sorts the characters in ascending order based on their ASCII values. The `result.append(new String(chars)).append(" ")` line appends the sorted word and a space to the result string. The `result.toString().trim()` line returns the final result string, removing any trailing space.

