import java.util.*;
import java.lang.*;
import java.math.*;

class Solution {
    public int maxFill(List<List<Integer>> grid, int capacity) {
        int total = 0;
        for (List<Integer> row : grid) {
            int sum = 0;
            for (int num : row) {
                sum += num;
            }
            total += Math.ceil((double) sum / capacity);
        }
        return total;
    }
}
```

This Java code does the same thing as your Python code. It iterates over each row in the grid, sums the numbers in each row, and then divides that sum by the capacity. The result is rounded up to the nearest whole number using `Math.ceil()`. The sum of these rounded values is returned as the result.

Please note that in Java, we need to cast the sum to double before dividing it by capacity to ensure floating point division. If we don't do this, Java will perform integer division.

